      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "c19df1a91074c144ab43e8182af58724331fbad0",
            "subject": "LU-20565 tests: run sanity-ec with fewer OSTs"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-29 22:00:35.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-29 22:26:14.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: remove duplicate sanity-ec subtests",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: remove duplicate sanity-ec subtests\n\nMany sanity-ec degraded-read subtests repeated the same layout,\nwrite, resync and fault as another subtest.  They would add run time\nand setup cost without testing anything the other subtest did not.\n\nRemove each subtest whose checks another subtest already makes:\n\n- 11 (create 2+2): 12a creates the same layout and checks parity\n- 30a (write stales parity, resync): 23a and 28a check the same\n  ro/wp/stale transitions, 6b checks the data across the resync\n- 41f (DIO read after buffered write): 41i does that after a\n  buffered degraded read of the same file\n- 43c, 44c (EIO when all reads fail): 44a, which also reads the\n  file again after the fault is cleared\n- 43d (fail 1, then 2 stripes): 63c fails 1, then 2, then 1 again\n- 44b (repeat a 1-OST fault): 63a and 63c fail and clear faults\n  repeatedly on the same file\n- 45a (fail stripes 0 and 1): 43b is the same test\n- 45c (fail only parity OSTs): 75a, which now fails every parity\n  OST that holds no data rather than one, and also checks stat and\n  getstripe\n- 47a (2+1 then 4+2 PFL): 68d, which fails each safe OST in turn\n- 47c (1M then 4M stripe PFL): 46d\n- 47d (read across a PFL boundary): 42d\n- 63b (every pair of safe OSTs): 58a is the same test\n- 64b (stale parity read, then resync): 48c\n- 64c (3 rewrite/resync rounds from mount2): 64a does 2 rounds\n- 65a (3-component PFL): 65b uses 4 components of mixed geometry\n  and stripe size\n- 67b (rewrite and resync 3 times): 75b repeats overwrite, resync\n  and degraded read 50 times, and 64a covers truncating rewrites\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I8d081a238b2ef8f7d0b84b96514092ec773ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
